over a week in March there was chaos on  Turkey's border with Greece we watched  as migrants from the Middle East and  well beyond pushed at the European  Union's frontier they were encouraged  there by turkeys government told the  border would be open each had their own  motivation their own story the most  escaping war or poverty or both this is  the story of one of them shot and killed  here a faceless migrant whose death was  dismissed as fake news and whose life  was not a concern two months on we have  pieced together what we can a paper  trail conversations with family and  friends and a face with a name Mohammad  Gulzar this is the effect his death had  Sabich Ana's Muhammad's wife  we found her outside the hospital on the  day he was shot she had just identified  his body we now know that they were only  just married an hour earlier he had been  at the border fence with her shots were  fired seven people were hit the moments  were captured on multiple cameras filmed  by other migrants the footage has now  been collated by investigative teams  from independent fact-checking and open  source researchers at three  organizations Belen Kat forensic  architecture and light house reports and  with contributions from Sky News  specific events such as bursts of  gunfire acted as temporal indicators the  conclusion through audio-visual and  mapping analysis is that live rounds  were fired and that they came from the  direction of the Greek side  the Greek government in a statement to  us maintains their line from that day  that any suggestion they are responsible  is fake news a gross and deliberate  misinformation campaign generated by  Turkey Mohamed Gulzar we now know has a  son from a previous marriage happy to  talk to us but not comfortable showing  his identity he is suing the Greek state  for manslaughter and his lawyer has  advised him to remain anonymous our chat  and papers sent to us from his family  back in Pakistan reveals surprises  because it turns out Mohammed Gulzar had  actually lived in Greece for many years  our documents show that he was known to  the migration authorities he had a  long-standing application in for  residency his footprint there stretches  back to 2008 and his son lives and works  there now he had a job building and  maintaining home heaters he was friends  have said hard-working the money went  back to family in Pakistan which is his  son says why he left Greece at the  beginning of this year but on that same  trip he got married - it's been harder  to get clear answers here was this a  marriage of equal and genuine intentions  [Music]  this video was filmed by her  friend at the border they were all there  because they'd been told it was open the  clothes Mohammad Gulzar is wearing match  those worn when he was shot they all say  he approached the border fence to talk  to the Greek police he could speak Greek  and he wanted them to stop firing  teargas moments later he was shot the  Sun will soon submit legal documents to  the Greek courts they will contain  evidence from the investigation our  reports and these documents together  they tell the story of a heating  engineer from Pakistan whose life seemed  to be a journey to something better and  whose death no one will take  responsibility for mark stone Sky News
 

